sentences.t:
Ecce autem gemini a Tenedo tranquilla per alta—
horresco referens—immensis orbibus angues
incumbunt pelago, pariterque ad litora tendunt;

sentences.l:
Behold, however, twin, from Tenedos through the calm deeps —
I shudder, relating it — with immense coils, snakes
bear down on the sea, and together toward the shores make;

sentences.t:
et primum parva duorum
corpora natorum serpens amplexus uterque
implicat, et miseros morsu depascitur artus;

sentences.l:
and first the small of two
bodies of sons, each serpent, having embraced them,
winds about, and the wretched limbs with a bite feeds upon;

sentences.t:
Vertitur interea caelum et ruit oceano nox,
involvens umbra magna terramque polumque
Myrmidonumque dolos;

sentences.l:
The sky meanwhile turns, and night rushes from the ocean,
wrapping in great shadow both earth and heaven
and the Myrmidons' tricks;

and now the Argive phalanx, with ships drawn up in order, was going
from Tenedos, through the friendly silences of the quiet moon,
the known shores seeking,
